WEBVTT

02:49.460 --> 02:52.770
Original Work & Screenplay

02:49.460 --> 02:52.790
Kimura Yuuichi

02:53.690 --> 03:04.450
One Stormy Night

03:57.130 --> 03:58.760
Hey, Mei!

03:58.760 --> 04:00.560
It's time to head back!

04:09.020 --> 04:11.980
Looks like it's going to rain.

04:12.920 --> 04:14.360
Hold on!

04:23.740 --> 04:25.530
We have to hurry and get down from here!

04:25.530 --> 04:27.550
Hey, we're going on ahead!

04:28.040 --> 04:29.240
Mei, come on!

05:45.360 --> 05:48.260
I can't see a thing.

06:16.060 --> 06:17.770
Oh, heavens.

06:18.520 --> 06:21.460
It doesn't look like it's going to calm down anytime soon.

06:59.660 --> 07:01.360
<i>The sound of hooves...</i>

07:01.360 --> 07:03.470
<i>It's just a goat.</i>

07:05.490 --> 07:06.730
Quite a storm, isn't it?

07:08.430 --> 07:09.280
Huh?

07:09.280 --> 07:10.870
Someone else is here?

07:10.870 --> 07:12.410
'Scuse me, then.

07:12.410 --> 07:14.950
It was pitch black so I didn't notice you at all.

07:15.660 --> 07:19.000
l just ducked in here myself.

07:19.000 --> 07:21.020
I'm completely soaked.

07:22.520 --> 07:25.760
Jeez. Because of this mess, I twisted my ankle

07:25.760 --> 07:27.910
and got a good share of the rain myself.

07:37.050 --> 07:38.820
I'm quite relieved...

07:39.520 --> 07:41.690
that you came.

07:44.940 --> 07:47.050
Well, sure!

07:47.050 --> 07:53.520
On a stormy night like this, it'd get pretty lonely being alone in this pitch black barn.

08:06.590 --> 08:08.210
Are you all right?

08:08.210 --> 08:11.720
Figures, huh? I think I'm coming down with the sniffles.

08:11.720 --> 08:13.430
Me too.

08:13.430 --> 08:16.440
Thanks to that, I can't smell a thing.

08:19.410 --> 08:24.080
l guess all that we know right now is the sound of each other's voices.

08:35.180 --> 08:36.100
Um...

08:37.110 --> 08:39.410
Might I ask where do you live?

08:39.410 --> 08:40.770
Huh?

08:40.770 --> 08:43.410
l live out by Chomping Gorges.

08:43.410 --> 08:44.730
What?!

08:44.730 --> 08:46.800
Chomping Gorges?

08:51.820 --> 08:54.680
Isn't that place a bit dangerous?

08:54.680 --> 08:55.600
Oh?

08:55.600 --> 08:57.460
You think?

08:57.460 --> 09:01.640
Well, it is a little steep, but it's a nice place.

09:02.960 --> 09:05.320
You certainly are brave.

09:05.320 --> 09:07.650
l live near Pleasant Mountain.

09:07.650 --> 09:09.430
Oh!

09:11.740 --> 09:14.160
I'm pretty jealous.

09:14.160 --> 09:19.120
There must be a lot of good food out there!

09:31.800 --> 09:36.380
l prefer the food by Fluffy Valley myself.

09:36.890 --> 09:38.050
Oh, for sure.

09:38.050 --> 09:39.980
l go there frequently too!

09:39.980 --> 09:43.140
The food out there is a cut above, ain't it?

09:43.140 --> 09:44.150
Yes.

09:44.150 --> 09:45.640
It smells good.

09:45.640 --> 09:49.150
It's soft with a real nice texture.

09:49.150 --> 09:52.640
And it's so good you could eat there
every day and not get sick of it!

09:52.640 --> 09:53.600
You betcha.

09:53.600 --> 09:57.150
Once you've eaten there, you're completely hooked!

09:57.150 --> 10:02.080
Ah, if only I had some of that food right here and now!

10:02.080 --> 10:03.910
Indeed.

10:03.910 --> 10:05.580
l want to eat until I burst!

10:05.580 --> 10:06.630
That...

10:06.630 --> 10:08.000
delicious...

10:20.970 --> 10:25.600
Now that I think about it,
I was pretty skinny when I was a kid.

10:25.980 --> 10:29.230
l make it a point to eat like a horse now, but...

10:34.480 --> 10:35.940
<i>Come on, Gabu.</i>

10:35.940 --> 10:39.020
<i>You have to eat it or you won't grow big and strong!</i>

10:39.020 --> 10:41.120
<i>How many times do I have to tell you?</i>

10:41.120 --> 10:48.750
My mom had to stay on my case when I was young. Eat more, eat more!

10:48.750 --> 10:51.300
Oh, it was the same for me!

10:51.300 --> 10:54.210
She told me that if I don't eat properly when I have the chance,

10:54.210 --> 10:57.010
l won't be able to run fast when the time comes!

10:57.430 --> 10:59.080
Yeah, exactly.

10:59.080 --> 11:02.230
Mine said exactly the same thing.

11:02.230 --> 11:05.260
She told me I couldn't survive if I couldn't run fast!

11:06.840 --> 11:08.660
l was told exactly the same thing.

11:08.660 --> 11:12.770
But in my case it was by my grandmother, not my mother.

11:13.250 --> 11:14.460
Huh?

11:14.460 --> 11:15.770
Your grandmother?

11:16.320 --> 11:19.150
When I was very young, my mother...

11:19.150 --> 11:20.740
l see.

11:20.740 --> 11:23.780
My mom's dead now, too.

11:24.600 --> 11:26.160
Really?

11:26.160 --> 11:29.290
We're really alike, aren't we?

11:31.030 --> 11:32.160
You're right.

11:32.160 --> 11:34.980
We can't see each other's faces in the pitch black,

11:34.980 --> 11:37.550
but maybe even <i>those</i> look alike!

11:48.300 --> 11:52.050
l just kind of looked down on instinct.

11:52.050 --> 11:54.460
My face was probably lit up, though.

11:54.460 --> 11:55.710
Do we look alike?

11:57.050 --> 11:59.700
U-Uh, well...

11:59.700 --> 12:01.940
l shut my eyes without thinking about it.

12:09.000 --> 12:10.930
Oh, excuse me.

12:16.200 --> 12:19.680
Wow, I really can't handle this kind of noise.

12:23.140 --> 12:25.220
Me neither.

12:25.220 --> 12:28.890
Ah, that really surprised me.

12:29.190 --> 12:33.890
It looks like we really <i>are</i> alike, don't you think?

12:34.460 --> 12:38.900
You know, I was just thinking that we get along really well.

12:39.780 --> 12:42.060
I know! How about this...

12:42.060 --> 12:45.290
Someday, when the weather is good,
would you like to have lunch together?

12:45.290 --> 12:46.790
That'd be nice!

12:46.790 --> 12:49.980
l thought this was the worst night possible
thanks to that terrible storm,

12:49.980 --> 12:52.140
but I made a good friend.

12:52.140 --> 12:54.920
This might be the best night ever!

12:56.920 --> 12:57.920
Oh?

12:58.400 --> 13:00.800
It looks like the storm's lifted.

13:02.840 --> 13:03.800
You're right.

13:06.820 --> 13:08.800
Well, in that case,

13:08.800 --> 13:11.650
what do you think about lunch tomorrow?

13:11.650 --> 13:12.890
Sounds good!

13:14.260 --> 13:18.310
l always say the best weather comes after the storm!

13:18.310 --> 13:20.520
Where should we meet?

13:22.020 --> 13:25.320
How 'bout in front of this barn?

13:25.610 --> 13:26.580
It's decided!

13:26.580 --> 13:30.080
But neither of us knows what the other looks like.

13:30.080 --> 13:36.080
Then, just in case, I'll say, "I'm the one
you met one stormy night!"

13:37.680 --> 13:40.590
If you just say "one stormy night", I'll know it's you.

13:40.940 --> 13:46.590
Then our secret phrase will be "one stormy night."

13:51.520 --> 13:52.930
What's wrong?

13:53.280 --> 13:56.510
Oh, my foot fell asleep.

13:56.510 --> 13:57.940
Go ahead without me.

13:58.340 --> 14:01.740
Well, then, I'll see you tomorrow. "One stormy night!"

14:02.990 --> 14:04.660
One stormy night!

16:42.890 --> 16:48.230
<i>It looks like we really </i>are<i> alike, don't you think?</i>

17:17.870 --> 17:20.080
One stormy night!

17:21.780 --> 17:23.870
One stormy night!

17:56.360 --> 17:58.460
l was really surprised!

17:58.460 --> 18:00.930
l can't believe you're a wolf!

18:00.930 --> 18:02.660
Same here!

18:02.660 --> 18:06.740
Who woulda thought you'd be a goat?

18:06.740 --> 18:07.860
To tell the truth,

18:07.860 --> 18:14.220
l can't believe that I made plans to have lunch with a wolf.

18:14.220 --> 18:16.200
I can't, either!

18:16.200 --> 18:20.820
It's like having lunch <i>with</i> your lunch!

18:20.820 --> 18:22.660
Uh, beg yer pardon.

18:24.210 --> 18:25.660
It's all right.

18:26.070 --> 18:31.990
If you wanted to eat me, you would have
done it back in front of that barn, right?

18:31.990 --> 18:33.280
That's right!

18:33.280 --> 18:34.940
l may look this way,

18:34.940 --> 18:37.630
but I treasure friendship above all things.

18:38.120 --> 18:39.400
The same goes for me.

18:39.400 --> 18:41.470
My grandmother used to tell me all the time...

18:41.470 --> 18:43.640
"Take good care of your friends."

18:44.450 --> 18:45.560
Yeah.

18:45.560 --> 18:49.650
My mom said the same thing.

18:49.650 --> 18:50.780
Is that so?

18:55.040 --> 18:58.860
When you also consider how we're both scared of thunder,

18:59.220 --> 19:00.610
l guess we really are alike.

19:02.700 --> 19:04.270
You're absolutely right.

19:29.300 --> 19:30.730
It collapsed!

19:43.760 --> 19:45.370
Be careful, now.

19:46.760 --> 19:50.100
I'm used to cliffs like this.

19:59.130 --> 20:00.970
Oh, no!

20:05.430 --> 20:06.880
Well, whatever!

20:06.880 --> 20:11.020
It's nothing for me to go two or three days without eating!

20:11.020 --> 20:14.760
Last night, you said you always make a
point of eating like a horse, didn't you?

20:17.240 --> 20:19.540
Did I really say something like that?

20:28.870 --> 20:31.080
<i>When I realized I lost my lunch,</i>

20:31.080 --> 20:33.500
<i>l suddenly got hungry!</i>

21:03.520 --> 21:06.490
<i>It looks so tasty...</i>

21:42.920 --> 21:44.400
What's wrong?

21:46.300 --> 21:47.780
We're here.

21:50.200 --> 21:52.370
Look, we're at the peak!

22:06.140 --> 22:07.470
Oh, look!

22:07.470 --> 22:09.430
You can see Fluffy Valley!

22:09.430 --> 22:10.530
You're right!

22:10.530 --> 22:12.240
l go there a lot to get foo—

22:13.230 --> 22:14.340
Huh?

22:14.340 --> 22:15.650
Food?

22:15.650 --> 22:19.310
N-No, I never go there to eat!

22:20.860 --> 22:21.820
Really?

22:22.250 --> 22:23.590
Of course not!

22:23.590 --> 22:27.190
Ain't never eaten a single scrap of goat meat!

22:28.660 --> 22:30.480
l see.

22:31.050 --> 22:33.510
Well, let's have our lunch!

22:33.510 --> 22:36.160
Oh... you dropped yours, didn't you?

22:37.280 --> 22:38.620
Sure did.

22:40.000 --> 22:42.910
Would you care to share half of mine?

22:42.910 --> 22:45.840
l guess it has to be meat, though, right?

22:45.840 --> 22:47.780
Uh, well...

22:47.780 --> 22:52.680
Ah, maybe you had some goat meat
in the lunch you dropped earlier?

22:53.220 --> 22:55.060
O-Of course not!

22:55.060 --> 22:58.270
l really, really <i>hate</i> goat meat!

22:58.270 --> 23:01.060
It's obvious, isn't it?

23:01.070 --> 23:02.480
l guess you're right.

23:02.480 --> 23:03.900
Of course!

23:03.900 --> 23:07.380
Now, don't worry about me, eat up!

23:07.380 --> 23:09.720
I'm going to take a little nap or something.

23:10.220 --> 23:11.540
In that case...

23:15.150 --> 23:16.120
It looks so good!

23:25.840 --> 23:30.300
<i>l guess when I think about it,
I </i>do<i> kind of have a lunch with me.</i>

23:30.300 --> 23:32.220
<i>Right here in front of me...</i>

23:34.860 --> 23:39.910
Really, lunch tastes the best when you eat it while
gazing over this scenery, don't you think?

23:40.720 --> 23:41.810
I'm sorry.

23:41.810 --> 23:42.760
Oh?

23:42.760 --> 23:44.440
He's asleep already.

23:48.910 --> 23:51.370
<i>As if I could sleep.</i>

23:51.370 --> 23:54.450
<i>l haven't eaten anything all day!</i>

23:55.700 --> 23:57.500
I'm so full.

23:57.500 --> 24:00.920
It feels so nice... I think I'll take a nap, too.

24:35.670 --> 24:40.200
<i>He's a really nice guy.</i>

24:40.200 --> 24:42.420
<i>He'd be tasty to eat,</i>

24:42.420 --> 24:46.560
<i>but for whatever reason,
I feel real calm when he's around.</i>

24:46.560 --> 24:49.380
<i>Although he would taste good...</i>

24:49.380 --> 24:55.720
<i>After all, there ain't nothing better than goat meat.</i>

24:58.240 --> 25:01.400
<i>Maybe I'll just have a lil' nibble.</i>

25:01.400 --> 25:05.730
<i>"You're a friend, so have one of my ears."</i>

25:06.160 --> 25:08.900
There's no way he'd say that.

25:09.770 --> 25:12.760
But I just... can't...

25:21.660 --> 25:23.210
Stop it!

25:23.210 --> 25:24.830
That tickles!

25:25.460 --> 25:28.510
Ah, that was a nice nap!

25:28.510 --> 25:30.980
I'm rather ticklish.

25:30.980 --> 25:33.550
Especially around the ears!

25:34.640 --> 25:35.710
Huh?

25:35.710 --> 25:36.770
What's wrong?

25:36.770 --> 25:39.300
ls there something on my ears?

25:39.820 --> 25:42.520
Huh? Ah, uh, well...

25:42.520 --> 25:44.640
No, not really, nothing at all!

25:45.390 --> 25:46.360
You're an odd one.

25:46.360 --> 25:48.480
Well, shall we get going?

25:48.480 --> 25:50.390
Y-You're right!

26:25.120 --> 26:26.430
At this rate...

26:26.890 --> 26:28.370
Just as I thought...

26:29.560 --> 26:30.910
l can't...

26:30.910 --> 26:32.910
hold back!

26:36.080 --> 26:36.900
What is it?

26:37.620 --> 26:41.500
I-I forgot one very important thing!

26:43.410 --> 26:45.040
What is it?

26:46.250 --> 26:50.340
Ah, umm, I just got all worked up, and so...

26:51.040 --> 26:55.050
W-When do you want to meet next?

27:15.450 --> 27:18.170
Autumn will soon be upon us.

27:18.170 --> 27:24.120
Those dreadful wolves will come
after us goats, one after the other.

27:24.120 --> 27:27.530
In other words... basically...

27:28.710 --> 27:33.130
This will be the most dangerous time of the year.

27:33.590 --> 27:35.820
Be absolutely certain not to let your guard down.

27:43.630 --> 27:45.770
I'm all right.

27:47.480 --> 27:53.260
Avoid moving alone at all costs. Move about in groups instead...

27:54.790 --> 27:55.580
Mei!

27:55.580 --> 27:56.970
Where are you going?

28:00.650 --> 28:03.110
I smell something fishy.

28:03.110 --> 28:05.440
I-I don't.

28:05.440 --> 28:07.760
What are you doing over here?

28:07.760 --> 28:10.330
It looks like Mei is going somewhere.

28:10.900 --> 28:12.750
Where are you going, Mei?

28:13.460 --> 28:17.500
Ah, well... I kind of have plans at Breezy Pass.

28:17.500 --> 28:20.130
Breezy Pass?

28:20.490 --> 28:22.700
What do you think you're doing?

28:22.700 --> 28:25.140
That's the place where a goat was killed by a wolf,

28:25.140 --> 28:28.140
just the other day, in broad daylight!

28:28.780 --> 28:33.050
It's called Lunch Pass nowadays!

28:34.510 --> 28:37.150
It's too dangerous to go by yourself!

28:37.490 --> 28:40.650
But, well, um, my friend...

28:41.140 --> 28:42.290
Your friend?

28:42.290 --> 28:43.160
Who's that?

28:44.140 --> 28:48.300
Well, it's... someone I met the other day.

28:48.300 --> 28:50.580
He lives kind of far away, so...

28:50.850 --> 28:52.060
Oh?

28:52.060 --> 28:54.960
So, Mei, I guess we won't be seeing a lot of you.

28:54.960 --> 28:55.600
Huh?

28:55.600 --> 28:56.580
Yeah...

28:56.580 --> 29:02.180
Anyway, going to Breezy Pass all by yourself is too dangerous!

29:02.180 --> 29:06.320
The Elder just warned us about that!

29:06.320 --> 29:07.220
Yeah.

29:07.220 --> 29:08.710
But...

29:09.940 --> 29:11.220
No, Mei.

29:11.220 --> 29:12.870
Absolutely not.

29:12.870 --> 29:15.730
If you're going to go, take Tap with you.

29:16.360 --> 29:17.730
Granny...

29:17.730 --> 29:21.510
Mei, if the unthinkable happened to you, l...

29:22.070 --> 29:25.240
l couldn't face your mother!

29:25.240 --> 29:28.990
Please. I'm asking you not to do anything dangerous.

29:28.990 --> 29:30.300
But, you know...

29:31.610 --> 29:33.210
That's right, Mei!

29:33.210 --> 29:35.040
I'll go with you!

29:35.720 --> 29:37.540
I'll go too!

29:38.260 --> 29:40.470
Look after Mei!

29:41.340 --> 29:42.580
We've got it covered!

29:42.580 --> 29:44.350
Now, let's go, Mei!

29:46.300 --> 29:47.430
Listen up, Mei.

29:47.430 --> 29:51.510
I can see that look on your face,
but it's a good thing I came with you!

29:52.000 --> 29:54.940
Ask me anything about wolves!

29:57.070 --> 30:00.150
What's that sigh supposed to mean?

30:01.660 --> 30:05.940
Hey, Mei, wolves are something you
can't let your guard down around!

30:05.940 --> 30:09.760
You'll run into trouble if you don't take precautions!

30:38.980 --> 30:43.150
That's right—there's a fragrant olive tree at the top of the pass, right?

30:43.150 --> 30:46.210
We'll hide ourselves and wait in the bushes under that tree.

30:46.210 --> 30:48.950
The olive tree has a strong smell to it.

30:48.950 --> 30:52.040
It'll hide our scents, right?

30:52.040 --> 30:52.780
Oh?

30:52.780 --> 30:55.160
Mii, you got it!

31:18.020 --> 31:21.010
It looks like your friend isn't here yet.

31:21.010 --> 31:21.840
Huh?

31:21.840 --> 31:22.860
Y-Yeah...

31:27.650 --> 31:29.010
Hey, Mei!

31:30.700 --> 31:32.810
What are you staring off at?

31:32.810 --> 31:33.370
Huh?

31:33.370 --> 31:34.620
Um, nothing.

31:35.220 --> 31:40.600
You know, when it comes to wolves,
I'm not just book-smart.

31:40.600 --> 31:42.400
I've seen them <i>tons</i> of times!

31:42.400 --> 31:44.920
But when you look at a wolf up close,

31:44.920 --> 31:49.570
their eyes shine, their mouths are filthy, their noses look funny...

31:49.570 --> 31:52.330
They're really ugly beyond hope!

31:58.890 --> 31:59.780
Feh.

31:59.780 --> 32:02.820
They're amateurs to think I'd be scared at something like that!

32:02.820 --> 32:05.290
Well, if a wolf should happen to show up,

32:05.290 --> 32:09.360
I'd stab it with my horns like this,
and then I'd use my hind legs to...

32:22.800 --> 32:25.750
It's here!

32:23.880 --> 32:25.750
H-Help us!

32:31.420 --> 32:33.490
That hurt!

32:33.490 --> 32:36.820
It just suddenly went and kicked me in the head!

32:37.810 --> 32:39.230
Sorry, sorry.

32:39.230 --> 32:42.160
Those were my friends just now.

32:43.710 --> 32:45.810
l see.

32:45.810 --> 32:51.060
They look like really tast... I mean, really nice friends.

32:51.060 --> 32:54.070
But, it looks like I kind of gave them a scare.

32:55.200 --> 32:58.360
But now, it's finally just the two of us.

32:59.080 --> 33:03.000
They were determined to come along because
they were "worried about Mei,"

33:03.000 --> 33:04.580
and I didn't know what to do!

33:04.580 --> 33:08.210
Oh, my name is Mei.

33:08.210 --> 33:09.120
Oh?

33:09.120 --> 33:10.800
"Mei," is it?

33:10.800 --> 33:13.590
Such a gentle-sounding name.

33:13.970 --> 33:16.340
I'm Gabu.

33:16.340 --> 33:18.890
Such a strong-sounding name!

33:18.890 --> 33:21.540
But it's kind of strange, isn't it?

33:21.540 --> 33:24.580
Not telling each other our names until now.

33:24.580 --> 33:25.860
That's true!

33:27.100 --> 33:30.110
By the way, had you been waiting long?

33:30.110 --> 33:33.130
Nope. Just got here myself.

33:37.790 --> 33:44.240
Anyway, my friends made quite a fuss.
If they knew that I was meeting a wolf...

33:44.820 --> 33:47.490
It's the same for me.

33:47.490 --> 33:51.710
There's no way I can tell the other fellas that I'm friends with a goat!

33:52.300 --> 33:55.130
It's a secret between just the two of us, isn't it?

33:55.610 --> 33:59.970
W-When you put it that way, it makes me all nervous!

33:59.970 --> 34:02.970
But is it really all right?

34:04.230 --> 34:05.520
You ask me that...

34:05.520 --> 34:07.740
But is it really all right with <i>you?</i>

34:07.740 --> 34:10.730
Being friends with a goat like me?

34:10.730 --> 34:14.360
That's why we're secret friends, right?

34:14.700 --> 34:16.090
That's right.

34:16.090 --> 34:18.210
We're secret friends, all right!

34:36.380 --> 34:39.450
Why did you leave Mei behind and run away?

34:39.450 --> 34:42.810
Why are you even asking that?
A wolf came out of nowhere!

34:42.810 --> 34:45.300
Anyone would've run!

34:45.300 --> 34:48.440
You're the one who said,
"I'll handle the wolves!", didn't you?

34:48.440 --> 34:50.400
T-That's true, but...

34:52.400 --> 34:55.860
A real, live wolf came out!

34:55.860 --> 34:56.650
Geez.

34:57.040 --> 34:59.660
What are you going to do if Mei gets eaten?

35:00.090 --> 35:01.440
You're right.

35:01.440 --> 35:03.410
What should we do?

35:03.410 --> 35:04.660
What are <i>you</i> going to do?

35:06.570 --> 35:07.960
Oh, it's Mei!

35:16.260 --> 35:17.380
Thank goodness!

35:17.380 --> 35:19.460
You didn't get eaten!

35:19.460 --> 35:21.890
Mei, hurry up!

35:21.890 --> 35:23.020
Mii!

35:23.020 --> 35:24.160
Tap!

35:51.120 --> 35:54.250
Meet at Crumbling Hills, huh?

35:56.230 --> 35:57.210
Hey, Gabu!

35:57.210 --> 35:58.460
What are you doing?

35:58.460 --> 36:00.970
Giro is about to give his speech!

36:03.300 --> 36:04.900
All right, Barry.

36:04.900 --> 36:05.970
I'm on my way.

36:21.960 --> 36:24.070
<i>Crumbling Hills it is.</i>

36:26.330 --> 36:27.950
I hope we're all on the same page.

36:28.620 --> 36:31.120
Failure in the upcoming hunt will not be tolerated.

36:31.120 --> 36:34.140
After all, when winter arrives, food will be hard to come by.

36:35.340 --> 36:39.130
We have to capture all our prey while we can—at all costs.

36:39.130 --> 36:40.180
Understood?

36:40.180 --> 36:42.340
Prepare yourselves!

36:41.370 --> 36:42.340
Yes, sir!

36:42.930 --> 36:44.880
We're going to start right away

36:44.880 --> 36:46.970
with a goat hunt at Crumbling Hills.

36:47.390 --> 36:50.140
<i>Gah! C-Crumbling Hills?</i>

36:50.680 --> 36:52.770
Crumbling Hills?

36:52.770 --> 36:56.230
Giro, there ain't many goats way out there!

36:58.280 --> 37:01.230
That's why we're going to Crumbling Hills.

37:01.230 --> 37:03.490
The hills there are entirely made of craggy rocks,

37:03.490 --> 37:06.140
but there is grass growing between them.

37:06.140 --> 37:09.490
And it seems that the goats find that grass very tasty.

37:10.510 --> 37:14.370
From what I saw, a number of goats will come in small groups.

37:15.290 --> 37:19.130
And they're not expecting us to go after them at a place like that.

37:19.130 --> 37:21.170
They will be caught completely off guard.

37:22.130 --> 37:23.340
l see!

37:23.340 --> 37:24.910
You're amazing, Giro!

37:24.910 --> 37:28.640
You gotta think differently when it comes to goat hunting!

37:29.060 --> 37:31.640
So, what's the plan, huh?

37:31.640 --> 37:35.480
Barry, your group will chase the goats, same as always.

37:35.480 --> 37:36.830
You know what I mean, right?

37:38.400 --> 37:41.210
Be sure to sneak up and surround them.

37:41.210 --> 37:41.900
All right?

37:41.900 --> 37:43.440
Yes, sir!

37:43.440 --> 37:44.910
Zack, Beach.

37:44.910 --> 37:46.910
You circle around the opposite side.

37:47.280 --> 37:48.830
It's a pinch operation.

37:48.830 --> 37:50.160
Yes, sir!

37:48.830 --> 37:50.160
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah!

37:50.160 --> 37:54.910
Simply follow my directions,
and the goats will be ours.

37:54.910 --> 37:57.170
Understood!

37:59.470 --> 38:03.520
<i>It looks like I gotta find a way to at least let Mei escape!</i>

38:12.470 --> 38:14.640
What an incredible place.

38:14.640 --> 38:17.320
This is the first time I've been out here.

38:21.360 --> 38:23.220
l wonder if Gabu is here.

38:24.730 --> 38:27.280
Gabuuu!

38:28.330 --> 38:29.220
Oh, no!

38:30.250 --> 38:33.430
l can't let myself be heard by any other wolves!

38:33.880 --> 38:35.620
But Gabu would...

38:38.980 --> 38:42.300
<i>If anything happens, call me right away!</i>

38:42.300 --> 38:44.650
<i>I'll be there to help in a jiffy!</i>

38:45.060 --> 38:48.640
<i>I may not look it, but I'm
something to be reckoned with!</i>

38:48.640 --> 38:50.320
<i>If I threaten them with a scary face,</i>

38:50.320 --> 38:54.290
<i>all of the other wolves will start shaking in their paws!</i>

38:54.290 --> 38:56.400
<i>Look, just like this!</i>

38:56.400 --> 39:01.530
<i>Graaaah!</i>

39:02.040 --> 39:04.510
Gabu's face was just...

39:34.760 --> 39:36.930
What a fog!

39:36.930 --> 39:40.940
At this rate, forget about hunting them—
it'll be hard to even <i>find</i> the goats, Giro!

39:41.450 --> 39:42.530
All right.

39:42.530 --> 39:44.780
Everyone split up and search.

39:45.610 --> 39:49.240
When you've found some prey, bark once as a sign.

39:49.240 --> 39:50.280
Yes, sir!

40:00.600 --> 40:02.860
<i>Where is he?</i>

40:03.880 --> 40:05.110
<i>Mei...</i>

40:08.400 --> 40:09.510
Hmm?

40:09.510 --> 40:11.470
l heard something.

40:12.140 --> 40:13.240
Maybe it's Gabu.

40:24.010 --> 40:26.210
l thought I just heard a goat's voice.

40:34.620 --> 40:35.420
<i>Oh!</i>

40:35.420 --> 40:36.720
<i>That's not Gabu!</i>

40:37.460 --> 40:38.600
<i>What should I do?</i>

40:42.500 --> 40:43.820
Dammit.

40:43.820 --> 40:47.670
The wind is blowing in different directions
and it's hard to make out any scents,

40:47.670 --> 40:50.500
but there's a goat nearby, no doubt.

41:05.760 --> 41:08.780
l smelled him right away when I came over here...

41:08.780 --> 41:10.030
Oh, Giro!

41:10.030 --> 41:10.610
What?

41:11.280 --> 41:13.040
Did you find something?

41:12.450 --> 41:13.040
Shh!

41:13.540 --> 41:15.300
Don't talk so loud.

41:15.910 --> 41:17.620
There's a goat nearby.

41:17.620 --> 41:18.780
What?

41:18.780 --> 41:19.800
A goat?

41:20.440 --> 41:21.620
<i>Could it be...</i>

41:22.290 --> 41:24.740
Well, I found some, too!

41:24.740 --> 41:26.540
Right over there in that rocky area!

41:26.540 --> 41:28.920
Plump, juicy-looking ones!

41:28.920 --> 41:30.630
Just thought I would let you know.

41:31.600 --> 41:33.220
Plump ones, huh?

41:33.220 --> 41:34.630
All right, I'll go.

41:36.990 --> 41:38.440
You keep watch here.

41:38.440 --> 41:39.180
Yessir!

41:41.180 --> 41:42.260
Me...

41:42.260 --> 41:43.640
Ah, Me...

41:43.640 --> 41:45.030
There we go...

41:45.740 --> 41:47.660
Ah... ah...

42:02.580 --> 42:03.920
Oh crap, look out!

42:44.440 --> 42:46.440
They won't find us now.

42:50.410 --> 42:52.430
Thank goodness!

42:52.430 --> 42:55.710
l don't know what I woulda done if they'd got you!

42:55.710 --> 42:57.550
Thank you, Gabu.

42:57.550 --> 43:00.470
You saved me, just like you promised.

43:01.030 --> 43:02.470
That's what friends do!

43:02.850 --> 43:06.900
But chasing goats is what <i>wolves</i> do, isn't it?

43:06.900 --> 43:08.980
For our meat, right?

43:10.140 --> 43:11.670
l guess you're right!

43:13.450 --> 43:17.780
But right now, instead of the goat meat...

43:19.560 --> 43:21.780
l prefer the goat.

43:23.420 --> 43:24.490
Gabu...

43:39.030 --> 43:41.180
It's quiet outside now.

43:42.350 --> 43:45.180
But the mist has gotten thick again.

43:46.220 --> 43:49.030
It's fortunate that I wasn't found, thanks to you.

43:49.800 --> 43:54.800
Maybe so, but the real reason I called you to this hill

43:54.800 --> 43:57.190
is that there's a full moon tonight.

43:58.500 --> 43:59.950
A full moon?

44:00.800 --> 44:05.200
l used to come here all the time to look at the moon.

44:05.200 --> 44:09.440
It looks so beautiful from here.

44:09.440 --> 44:11.180
Man!

44:11.180 --> 44:13.520
l wanted to show you, too...

44:13.520 --> 44:19.720
When you look at that moon, all the bad stuff on your mind just melts away!

44:20.390 --> 44:23.110
It doesn't look like we can see the moon tonight,

44:23.110 --> 44:28.720
but I can forget all the bad stuff just by talking with you, Gabu.

44:29.080 --> 44:31.900
R-Really?

44:31.900 --> 44:34.390
M-Me, too.

44:34.390 --> 44:37.110
Let's come here again to look at the full moon sometime.

44:39.280 --> 44:41.670
Okay.

45:02.180 --> 45:03.980
What's wrong, ma'am?

45:03.980 --> 45:05.600
What happened?

45:05.600 --> 45:07.980
T-The...

45:07.980 --> 45:11.180
The wolves attacked as a pack at Crumbling Hills!

45:11.180 --> 45:14.190
What? At Crumbling Hills?!

45:14.190 --> 45:18.190
I've never heard of wolves going there before.

45:18.740 --> 45:22.160
l was with the other mountain goats,

45:22.160 --> 45:25.630
but the wolves came in a pack and we were in trouble!

45:25.630 --> 45:27.990
Really? How many did they get?

45:27.990 --> 45:29.600
How am I supposed to know?

45:29.600 --> 45:31.950
l had my hands full with running away myself!

45:31.950 --> 45:34.150
They've been thinking, too.

45:34.150 --> 45:37.300
They went after the place where we let down our guard.

45:37.300 --> 45:39.960
It'll be winter soon—they're getting desperate, too.

45:40.430 --> 45:41.840
Oh, that's right, that's right!

45:41.840 --> 45:43.330
Speaking of everything going crazy,

45:43.330 --> 45:47.370
while I was running away,
I saw something unbelievable!

45:47.370 --> 45:49.600
What do you mean, "unbelievable"?

45:49.600 --> 45:50.470
What did you see?

45:50.470 --> 45:51.970
It was...

45:51.970 --> 45:57.480
In the middle of that ruckus, a goat and a wolf were running away, holding hands like they were pals or something!

45:57.480 --> 45:58.690
What?

45:58.690 --> 46:00.480
A goat and a wolf?

46:01.060 --> 46:01.940
It can't be.

46:01.940 --> 46:02.990
There's no way!

46:03.370 --> 46:06.610
l couldn't believe it at first, either!

46:06.610 --> 46:10.490
l completely forgot about running away and just stared!

46:10.820 --> 46:11.440
What?

46:11.440 --> 46:12.370
It's true?

46:12.370 --> 46:13.870
l can't believe it...

46:13.870 --> 46:16.500
So, what does it mean?

46:16.500 --> 46:18.950
And that goat!

46:18.950 --> 46:22.800
l thought I had seen him somewhere before
and realized it was Mei, of all goats!

46:22.800 --> 46:23.800
What?!

46:23.800 --> 46:24.510
Mei?!

46:24.510 --> 46:26.460
l can't believe it.

46:25.360 --> 46:26.460
It was Mei?

46:26.460 --> 46:30.510
Now that you mention it, he's been gone a lot recently.

46:31.310 --> 46:34.880
By the way, where is Mei now?

46:34.880 --> 46:38.230
Now that you mention it,
I haven't seen him since last night.

46:38.230 --> 46:41.400
Ahh, I don't even want to <i>remember</i> it!

46:41.400 --> 46:41.440
Ahh, I don't even want to <i>remember</i> it!

46:41.440 --> 46:41.480
Ahh, I don't even want to <i>remember</i> it!

46:41.480 --> 46:41.520
Ahh, I don't even want to <i>remember</i> it!

46:41.520 --> 46:41.570
Ahh, I don't even want to <i>remember</i> it!

46:41.570 --> 46:41.610
Ahh, I don't even want to <i>remember</i> it!

46:41.610 --> 46:41.650
Ahh, I don't even want to <i>remember</i> it!

46:43.760 --> 46:45.070
Geez.

46:45.070 --> 46:47.490
The hunt yesterday was terrible!

46:47.490 --> 46:49.950
There wasn't much you could do in all that fog.

46:49.950 --> 46:52.890
l had that feast right in front of my eyes, too...

46:52.890 --> 46:54.200
Hey!

46:55.440 --> 46:56.620
Where's Gabu?

47:00.040 --> 47:03.250
Actually, I haven't seen him since last night.

47:03.250 --> 47:07.720
Gabu was assigned to chasing goats with you, wasn't he?

47:07.720 --> 47:14.220
Yes, well, he just vanished in the middle of all that mess.

47:15.920 --> 47:19.960
Moving on your own is forbidden during our hunts.

47:19.960 --> 47:21.240
l can't let that slip.

47:21.240 --> 47:22.610
Call Gabu right away!

47:22.610 --> 47:26.570
Uh, well, we don't know where he went, so...

47:26.570 --> 47:29.430
Then separate into groups and find him right away!

47:29.430 --> 47:30.530
Yes, sir!

47:42.250 --> 47:43.380
Huh?

47:43.380 --> 47:45.320
What's wrong, everyone?

47:45.320 --> 47:47.340
You're making such scary faces.

47:57.200 --> 47:58.890
Did I do something?

48:01.430 --> 48:06.270
Mei, I heard you've made friends with a wolf.

48:06.650 --> 48:07.390
<i>What?</i>

48:08.280 --> 48:16.160
ls it true that while the goats were being
attacked one after another by wolves,

48:16.160 --> 48:19.410
you were holding hands with one of them?

48:20.340 --> 48:21.500
It's a lie, right?

48:21.500 --> 48:23.250
Hey, Mei, it's a lie, isn't  it!

48:23.250 --> 48:23.930
Please!

48:23.930 --> 48:25.420
Say it's a lie!

48:28.860 --> 48:30.420
It's true.

48:31.180 --> 48:32.240
Mei!

48:34.770 --> 48:36.810
l see. I get it now!

48:36.810 --> 48:38.330
It's the wolf from back then!

48:38.330 --> 48:40.930
The one who appeared at Breezy Pass!

48:41.730 --> 48:45.320
We were thankful that you didn't get eaten,

48:45.320 --> 48:47.860
but you mean to say that was your friend?

48:50.780 --> 48:53.110
Well, Mei?

48:53.110 --> 48:57.950
He... that wolf is a really great guy!

48:58.440 --> 48:59.950
A wolf is a good guy?

49:00.790 --> 49:02.460
What are you thinking?

49:02.730 --> 49:05.460
Wolves eat us!

49:05.460 --> 49:06.420
That's right!

49:06.420 --> 49:08.820
What do you mean friends?

49:10.170 --> 49:14.160
Now, Mei, I don't understand all of the circumstances,

49:14.160 --> 49:17.930
but from their point of view,
we're nothing more than food.

49:18.480 --> 49:21.750
They live by eating us.

49:21.750 --> 49:23.460
Do you think that such a creature...

49:26.740 --> 49:29.770
would be our friend?

49:30.240 --> 49:31.420
That's right, Mei!

49:31.420 --> 49:32.720
Can we...

49:34.520 --> 49:37.580
...become friends with this grass?

49:37.580 --> 49:39.030
Look at it!

49:39.030 --> 49:43.120
No matter what you do, it only looks like tasty food!

49:44.780 --> 49:49.130
He's different from the other wolves.

49:49.510 --> 49:52.630
That wolf's pulling the wool over your eyes!

49:52.630 --> 49:54.790
That's right, Mei.

49:54.790 --> 49:55.600
Listen to me.

49:55.600 --> 50:00.640
From their point of view, you are a convenient
meal that can be called upon at any time.

50:01.020 --> 50:03.140
No, that's not all.

50:03.590 --> 50:08.080
Where we are at all times, where we go to eat...

50:09.900 --> 50:14.370
Where the weaker goats are resting, hidden away...

50:14.370 --> 50:17.940
They may intend to extract all of this from you.

50:18.660 --> 50:20.070
That's right, Mei!

50:20.070 --> 50:23.750
They could even lure us out one by one and eat us!

50:23.750 --> 50:27.320
If that happened, it'd be the end for us!

50:30.140 --> 50:32.880
Gabu, do you understand what you've done?

50:33.640 --> 50:34.990
Huh? Have I done some—

50:34.990 --> 50:36.390
Don't play dumb!

50:36.390 --> 50:41.730
Not only did you stop me from grabbing that one back in the fog,

50:41.730 --> 50:45.680
you actually helped it escape, didn't you?

50:47.260 --> 50:48.400
Well?

50:51.360 --> 50:52.220
Well...

50:52.220 --> 50:55.110
Stop mumbling and spit it out!

50:55.110 --> 51:01.480
Uh, okay... but he... that goat is a really great guy!

51:02.500 --> 51:03.290
What?

51:03.290 --> 51:04.500
ls he serious?

51:03.460 --> 51:04.500
A goat?

51:04.500 --> 51:05.770
What crap.

51:05.770 --> 51:07.700
Are you stupid?!

51:07.700 --> 51:09.750
Goats are our food!

51:09.750 --> 51:12.420
Who gives a damn whether that food is a great guy?!

51:12.420 --> 51:14.260
Hey, Gabu.

51:14.260 --> 51:19.430
Goats, cows, pigs, birds, rabbits... they're all our food.

51:18.490 --> 51:19.430
Food, food!

51:19.430 --> 51:23.810
If we make friends with our food, we'll starve to death!

51:23.810 --> 51:26.810
What do you plan on eating to survive?

51:26.810 --> 51:27.770
That's right, that's right!

51:27.770 --> 51:32.450
W-Well, that's... It's fine if it's just him.

51:32.450 --> 51:34.450
ls one single goat really going to—

51:34.450 --> 51:36.630
Use your freaking head, Gabu!

51:36.630 --> 51:39.620
Even if you make friends with just him,

51:39.620 --> 51:42.520
you'll end up talkin' about everything with him!

51:42.520 --> 51:44.890
Where we wolves are,

51:44.890 --> 51:48.420
where and when we're gonna be hunting,

51:48.420 --> 51:51.060
even what strategy we'll use!

51:51.060 --> 51:55.090
He'll find out all about them, and we'll starve to death!

51:55.090 --> 51:58.640
But we've never talked about that even once!

51:58.640 --> 52:00.300
Cut the crap!

52:00.790 --> 52:03.100
You still don't get it?

52:03.100 --> 52:05.980
You're being used by them!

52:05.980 --> 52:09.270
You've already helped one of them.

52:09.980 --> 52:11.310
That's not...

52:12.200 --> 52:14.000
Listen, Gabu.

52:14.000 --> 52:19.170
Those goats. Do you think they would really
become friends with wolves like us,

52:19.170 --> 52:21.820
who kill and eat their friends?

52:23.910 --> 52:25.080
All right.

52:25.080 --> 52:28.000
Until Gabu's punishment is decided,

52:28.000 --> 52:30.560
lock him up in a cave at Valley's Bottom.

52:29.610 --> 52:30.560
Yes, sir!

52:41.680 --> 52:43.670
That's true.

52:43.670 --> 52:46.060
I'm a goat, after all.

52:46.060 --> 52:47.890
It's just as everyone says.

52:55.740 --> 52:57.070
Now that I think of it,

52:57.070 --> 53:01.370
Gabu said that the food at Fluffy Valley
was his favorite, didn't he?

53:03.380 --> 53:06.280
That's because he's a wolf, after all.

53:07.340 --> 53:11.890
l wouldn't be surprised if he'd killed
and eaten the goats there before.

53:13.060 --> 53:17.550
Oh, but he said that he really hates goat meat!

53:19.330 --> 53:22.170
Mei, are you awake?

53:22.800 --> 53:23.960
Granny.

53:24.480 --> 53:27.180
l couldn't sleep for the life of me.

53:30.740 --> 53:35.080
l came here because I thought it would
be better to tell you something now.

53:35.080 --> 53:36.140
What is it?

53:36.140 --> 53:38.690
It's about your mother.

53:39.060 --> 53:39.820
What?

53:39.820 --> 53:40.690
About Mom?

53:40.690 --> 53:41.960
Yes.

53:41.960 --> 53:45.410
She always followed you everywhere.

53:45.410 --> 53:48.410
She loved you more than anything else.

53:48.410 --> 53:49.680
l remember that.

53:50.460 --> 53:52.460
Kind of...

53:52.460 --> 53:59.130
When you were very young, she was
killed by wolves while protecting you.

53:59.130 --> 54:00.590
By wolves?!

54:00.590 --> 54:01.300
Yes.

54:01.300 --> 54:06.810
She was brave, though,
and bit off one of the wolves' ears.

54:06.810 --> 54:11.060
But in the end, the wolves ate her.

54:11.410 --> 54:12.730
l see...

54:12.730 --> 54:14.480
So that's what happened...

54:35.490 --> 54:36.420
<i>Hey!</i>

54:36.420 --> 54:37.090
<i>C'mon!</i>

54:37.090 --> 54:38.370
<i>What's wrong?</i>

54:38.370 --> 54:40.380
<i>C'mon, hurry up!</i>

54:40.380 --> 54:42.430
<i>Stop stalling!</i>

54:42.430 --> 54:44.300
<i>Anyone can do this!</i>

54:44.300 --> 54:46.770
<i>The sun's going to set before you do this!</i>

54:46.770 --> 54:48.220
<i>Hurry up, already!</i>

54:48.220 --> 54:50.140
<i>What are you so scared of?</i>

54:50.140 --> 54:51.230
What's wrong?

54:51.230 --> 54:53.140
You're all ruffled, Gabu!

54:53.140 --> 54:55.640
Stop taking forever!

54:55.640 --> 54:57.670
Hey, hurry up and jump!

54:57.670 --> 54:59.470
You're a wolf, ain't you?

54:59.470 --> 55:00.650
Hurry and get over here!

55:13.540 --> 55:15.540
You call yourself a <i>wolf</i>?!

55:58.750 --> 56:00.330
Now, Mei...

56:01.740 --> 56:05.590
Did you manage to think things over
more rationally during the night?

56:05.590 --> 56:07.540
Uh... yes.

56:09.050 --> 56:11.890
l have also been thinking a lot.

56:11.890 --> 56:14.910
That wolf that you've gotten so close to...

56:16.770 --> 56:19.230
Would you like to see him again?

56:19.230 --> 56:20.440
What?

56:20.440 --> 56:21.390
See Gabu?

56:21.390 --> 56:23.150
Yes, that's right.

56:23.150 --> 56:26.860
Essentially, if they intend to use you,

56:26.860 --> 56:31.000
then we will do the opposite and use him.

56:32.330 --> 56:37.250
You are to meet with the wolf, smiling like everything is well.

56:37.250 --> 56:39.960
Where the wolves are. How many are in the pack.

56:39.960 --> 56:42.210
The places they never go.

56:42.210 --> 56:46.280
Their plans for future hunts... get them out of him!

56:48.250 --> 56:53.060
If you do so, then you will be one of us,
like you have been in the past.

56:53.060 --> 56:54.240
What do you think?

56:59.020 --> 57:00.290
l understand.

57:00.940 --> 57:02.200
l'll do it.

57:28.970 --> 57:30.720
Hey there, Gabu.

57:30.720 --> 57:32.010
Have you cooled your head?

57:33.010 --> 57:33.680
Yeah...

57:34.520 --> 57:36.640
Your punishment's been handed down!

57:37.600 --> 57:38.640
Yeah?

57:39.100 --> 57:41.510
In accordance with the code of the wolves,

57:42.190 --> 57:44.140
you are to be put to death.

57:47.150 --> 57:48.530
However!

57:49.550 --> 57:53.530
There is the fact that your father was my best friend.

57:53.530 --> 57:58.000
So I decided to make an exception
and give you a special chance.

57:58.540 --> 57:59.280
Okay...

57:59.710 --> 58:02.750
That goat you got along with so well...

58:02.750 --> 58:04.290
Meet him once more.

58:04.290 --> 58:05.380
What?

58:05.380 --> 58:07.290
W-With Mei?!

58:07.290 --> 58:08.460
That's right.

58:08.460 --> 58:14.300
Put on a nice face and wring him for
information about the goats.

58:15.790 --> 58:17.430
Sounds great, huh?

58:17.430 --> 58:19.850
We're gonna spare your life!

58:19.850 --> 58:23.980
All you gotta do is be sure and find out what they're doing,

58:23.980 --> 58:29.810
and we'll be able to get enough food without breaking a sweat!

58:30.240 --> 58:31.650
Listen up, Gabu.

58:31.650 --> 58:33.200
You only have one chance.

58:33.200 --> 58:36.480
If it looks like you're thinking of doing something stupid again,

58:36.480 --> 58:37.910
there will be no mercy the next time.

58:38.600 --> 58:42.160
We will track traitors no matter where
they go and execute them.

58:42.680 --> 58:44.960
That is the code of the wolves.

58:44.960 --> 58:46.230
Got it?

58:46.840 --> 58:48.670
l-l understand.

59:00.300 --> 59:02.020
Hey, hey, did you hear?

59:02.020 --> 59:03.270
l did, I did!

59:03.270 --> 59:05.020
About the wolf and the goat, right?

59:05.020 --> 59:06.690
l hear they're going to meet by the riverbank!

59:06.690 --> 59:08.500
l wonder what's going to happen.

59:10.070 --> 59:12.550
Let's go and see!

59:42.470 --> 59:44.890
Uh, sorry I'm late.

59:45.560 --> 59:46.620
It's okay.

59:46.620 --> 59:49.100
l just got here myself.

59:51.070 --> 59:53.900
Mmm... What do you want to do today?

59:53.900 --> 59:55.570
G-Good question...

59:56.240 --> 59:59.680
Well, why don't we go down to the stream?

01:00:03.120 --> 01:00:04.370
Yeah.

01:00:04.370 --> 01:00:05.780
Why don't we do that?

01:00:58.890 --> 01:01:01.550
l wonder if Mei will be able to pull this off all right.

01:01:01.850 --> 01:01:03.030
Indeed.

01:01:03.030 --> 01:01:06.470
Our life as a clan is depending on it.

01:01:06.470 --> 01:01:08.840
We have no other choice but to hope he tries his best.

01:01:09.660 --> 01:01:12.060
This has turned into such a mess!

01:01:24.740 --> 01:01:26.030
That son of a gun.

01:01:26.710 --> 01:01:30.120
He got all chummy with a such a delicious-looking goat?

01:01:30.120 --> 01:01:31.140
l can't forgive that.

01:01:31.140 --> 01:01:33.170
Now, now, Giro.

01:01:33.170 --> 01:01:35.250
If Gabu works that goat real good,

01:01:35.250 --> 01:01:38.090
we can have all the goats we can eat!

01:01:38.580 --> 01:01:41.800
l get pissed off just looking at goats.

01:01:41.800 --> 01:01:44.170
I'm going to kill and eat every last one of them!

01:01:44.170 --> 01:01:46.890
Giro, please calm down.

01:01:46.890 --> 01:01:50.100
You always get worked up talking about goats.

01:01:50.420 --> 01:01:52.520
Shut your trap, damn you.

01:01:54.270 --> 01:01:55.530
All right, all right.

01:02:12.080 --> 01:02:13.660
It started raining.

01:02:30.300 --> 01:02:32.060
Aw, this stinks!

01:02:35.840 --> 01:02:37.310
Under that rock!

01:02:38.820 --> 01:02:39.810
All right.

01:02:51.000 --> 01:02:53.170
It's slippery, so watch out!

01:02:53.170 --> 01:02:54.120
Okay.

01:03:33.780 --> 01:03:35.040
Mei!

01:03:47.090 --> 01:03:47.920
Gabu!

01:04:14.180 --> 01:04:16.940
Jeez, you're as clumsy as always!

01:04:16.940 --> 01:04:19.460
If you slip in a place like this...

01:04:19.460 --> 01:04:20.420
l know.

01:04:20.420 --> 01:04:23.210
I've been careless like that since I was young.

01:04:29.090 --> 01:04:31.010
The truth is, l...

01:04:31.720 --> 01:04:33.320
While I've been here...

01:04:34.410 --> 01:04:39.600
I've been planning the whole time to deceive
you and find out about the goats.

01:04:39.880 --> 01:04:41.090
But l...

01:04:41.980 --> 01:04:46.110
Just as I thought, there's no way I could lie to you!

01:04:46.110 --> 01:04:47.690
I planned the same thing.

01:04:48.240 --> 01:04:51.410
But... well...

01:04:51.410 --> 01:04:54.620
When I saw your face, I knew I couldn't do it.

01:04:59.620 --> 01:05:03.370
l guess we really are secret friends, huh?

01:05:04.130 --> 01:05:05.900
Secret friends?

01:05:06.710 --> 01:05:08.340
l guess you're right.

01:05:09.730 --> 01:05:14.340
But... it doesn't look like it's a secret any more.

01:05:15.100 --> 01:05:16.180
You're right.

01:05:16.180 --> 01:05:19.020
We're in a pretty big pickle.

01:05:19.020 --> 01:05:20.350
What will we do?

01:05:20.850 --> 01:05:23.810
We either go forward or go back.

01:05:24.290 --> 01:05:28.270
Wouldn't eating me also be a way to end it?

01:05:30.720 --> 01:05:32.610
It'd be pretty simple if I could do that!

01:05:34.610 --> 01:05:37.580
How long are those two going to keep yapping?

01:05:37.580 --> 01:05:38.620
Dunno.

01:05:46.380 --> 01:05:51.010
Now that we've come this far,
why don't we go somewhere else?

01:05:51.010 --> 01:05:51.640
Sure.

01:05:51.640 --> 01:05:55.360
I've been prepared to do something
like that for a while now.

01:06:00.220 --> 01:06:04.730
Hey, with the river flowing like this,
it'll work out somehow!

01:06:04.730 --> 01:06:06.240
l guess you're right.

01:06:22.600 --> 01:06:23.500
Huh?

01:06:26.450 --> 01:06:29.440
Be certain to stay alive so we can meet again.

01:06:30.760 --> 01:06:32.450
Of course.

01:07:05.630 --> 01:07:07.160
Gabu!

01:07:22.430 --> 01:07:25.290
Mei!

01:08:38.930 --> 01:08:39.720
Mei?

01:08:41.850 --> 01:08:43.220
Mei!

01:08:46.060 --> 01:08:48.640
Mei! Mei!

01:08:49.650 --> 01:08:51.390
Mei!

01:08:52.450 --> 01:08:55.730
Mei! Mei!

01:08:58.200 --> 01:08:59.160
Mei...

01:08:59.990 --> 01:09:03.200
Oh... it's all my fault.

01:09:03.870 --> 01:09:05.830
If this was how it was going to turn out,

01:09:05.830 --> 01:09:09.900
It would have been better if he'd never met me!

01:09:13.380 --> 01:09:15.730
I'm glad I met you.

01:09:21.090 --> 01:09:22.300
Mei!

01:09:32.980 --> 01:09:36.900
To be able to meet like this again...
I feel like I'm dreaming!

01:09:38.440 --> 01:09:41.780
l thought we were done for last night, myself!

01:09:41.780 --> 01:09:46.240
l was so, so happy when I heard your voice, Gabu!

01:09:47.160 --> 01:09:50.740
Hey, aren't those two the goat and the wolf from last night?

01:09:51.380 --> 01:09:54.090
Yeah, they jumped in the river after all that, didn't they?

01:09:54.090 --> 01:09:55.590
I'm surprised they survived!

01:09:55.590 --> 01:09:57.170
l wonder what they're going to do now.

01:09:57.170 --> 01:09:58.230
Beats me...

01:10:01.130 --> 01:10:05.560
These rumors will reach the wolves before long.

01:10:05.560 --> 01:10:07.220
You're right.

01:10:07.220 --> 01:10:08.980
Where are they going?

01:10:08.980 --> 01:10:11.220
l can't believe a wolf and a goat are going off together.

01:10:36.190 --> 01:10:38.460
What are we gonna do now?

01:10:39.600 --> 01:10:42.600
Why don't we go to the other side of that mountain?

01:10:43.960 --> 01:10:46.220
T-That mountain?

01:10:46.220 --> 01:10:47.970
That mountain's, uh...

01:10:49.100 --> 01:10:52.640
No one's ever been to the other side of it.

01:10:52.640 --> 01:10:54.480
That's why we're going.

01:10:54.480 --> 01:10:58.110
We don't have any place to go back to, right?

01:10:58.110 --> 01:11:00.110
That's true, but...

01:11:00.880 --> 01:11:04.050
I'm sure it's there.

01:11:04.050 --> 01:11:07.250
Another green forest, on the other side of that mountain.

01:11:07.250 --> 01:11:09.110
A green forest?

01:11:09.110 --> 01:11:10.200
Yes.

01:11:10.800 --> 01:11:12.290
I'm sure it's there.

01:11:12.290 --> 01:11:16.670
It might be a forest where wolves and goats can live together.

01:11:17.640 --> 01:11:20.130
That'd be really something, wouldn't it?

01:11:20.840 --> 01:11:24.380
I'm sure the peak is covered in deep snow

01:11:24.380 --> 01:11:27.210
and that a cold strong enough to freeze you is waiting for us.

01:11:27.210 --> 01:11:30.540
It's not a walk in the park to get there, right?

01:11:30.540 --> 01:11:32.480
That's why no one goes there,

01:11:32.480 --> 01:11:35.140
and that's why no one comes from there.

01:11:36.310 --> 01:11:38.140
We'll make it somehow.

01:11:39.320 --> 01:11:40.740
You're right.

01:11:40.740 --> 01:11:43.320
l guess we really have no choice but to go there, right?

01:11:43.320 --> 01:11:45.150
There's gotta be one!

01:11:45.990 --> 01:11:47.820
A green forest...

01:11:47.820 --> 01:11:48.650
Yep!

01:12:21.690 --> 01:12:24.990
All right! We're going to split into two teams and search for them!

01:12:24.990 --> 01:12:25.900
Aye!

01:12:25.900 --> 01:12:27.320
Barry, your team goes to the north.

01:12:27.320 --> 01:12:28.190
Yes, sir!

01:12:28.610 --> 01:12:30.780
My team will search the east.

01:12:30.780 --> 01:12:31.780
Understood.

01:12:33.220 --> 01:12:34.680
Damn you, Gabu.

01:12:35.210 --> 01:12:37.670
It was a mistake to go easy on him.

01:12:37.670 --> 01:12:39.750
Protecting a goat, of all things...

01:12:39.750 --> 01:12:41.400
l can't forgive him.

01:12:41.400 --> 01:12:43.750
Be sure and find him, no matter what!

01:12:43.750 --> 01:12:47.470
'Course, once we've found him,
we'll execute him, yeah?

01:12:47.470 --> 01:12:50.200
But oh, that goat that was with him...

01:12:50.850 --> 01:12:52.760
He looked so delicious!

01:12:53.170 --> 01:12:54.300
Idiot!

01:12:54.300 --> 01:12:58.230
Mark my words. I'm not going to kill that goat so simply.

01:12:58.230 --> 01:12:59.200
Let's go!

01:13:07.900 --> 01:13:10.200
What's so funny?

01:13:10.200 --> 01:13:14.310
Well, it's just that the two of us can
spend every day together, right?

01:13:14.310 --> 01:13:15.220
Yeah.

01:13:15.830 --> 01:13:21.290
Up till now, I was always worried about
hurrying up to get back to the pack.

01:13:21.290 --> 01:13:22.190
That's right.

01:13:22.190 --> 01:13:25.630
Now, we can always be together.

01:13:25.630 --> 01:13:27.820
Just thinking about it is kind of fun!

01:13:28.300 --> 01:13:31.590
But we're being chased.

01:13:31.590 --> 01:13:33.890
Don't let your guard down!

01:13:33.890 --> 01:13:37.350
We're too visible here. It's dangerous.

01:13:37.350 --> 01:13:38.230
'Kay.

01:13:38.230 --> 01:13:40.310
I'll walk real carefully.

01:13:49.060 --> 01:13:52.610
This smell—it's Gabu and the goat.

01:13:52.610 --> 01:13:53.780
Hey!

01:13:53.780 --> 01:13:55.820
They may still be nearby!

01:13:55.820 --> 01:13:59.030
It looks like they came through here just a short while ago.

01:13:59.030 --> 01:14:00.370
There's goat hair scattered about.

01:14:00.370 --> 01:14:01.310
All right!

01:14:01.310 --> 01:14:03.380
Find out which way they went!

01:14:03.380 --> 01:14:04.410
Understood.

01:15:16.780 --> 01:15:19.530
How many did you kill today?

01:15:23.460 --> 01:15:25.900
About two or three field mice, I guess.

01:15:27.350 --> 01:15:32.540
Every night while I'm sleeping,
you go off and kill them, don't you?

01:15:33.690 --> 01:15:34.550
You know,

01:15:35.090 --> 01:15:37.400
even <i>l</i> get hungry!

01:15:37.400 --> 01:15:40.000
I'm doing this in the first place because I haven't eaten you.

01:15:40.550 --> 01:15:44.480
l know that you're being considerate
of me and doing it like that.

01:15:44.480 --> 01:15:46.600
But really...

01:15:46.600 --> 01:15:48.700
what you don't like, you don't like!

01:15:52.780 --> 01:15:55.560
Well, what <i>should</i> I do?

01:15:59.690 --> 01:16:02.750
Hey, did you just hear a voice?

01:16:02.750 --> 01:16:03.660
Yes!

01:16:03.660 --> 01:16:06.470
It sounded like it came from over here.

01:16:08.040 --> 01:16:10.460
But there's no scent.

01:16:10.460 --> 01:16:12.130
Maybe they're further downwind?

01:16:12.510 --> 01:16:13.340
Right!

01:16:13.340 --> 01:16:15.220
I'll go search that area.

01:16:19.570 --> 01:16:21.280
W-What is it?

01:16:21.680 --> 01:16:23.500
T-There's...

01:16:23.500 --> 01:16:24.510
What?

01:16:24.980 --> 01:16:28.640
...some really cute flowers blooming here!

01:16:28.940 --> 01:16:30.350
Oh, you're right.

01:16:31.570 --> 01:16:33.310
Be careful not to step on them.

01:16:33.310 --> 01:16:34.730
l know.

01:16:35.080 --> 01:16:38.780
Anyway, Gabu and his little friend should
be around here somewhere.

01:16:38.780 --> 01:16:39.800
Yeah!

01:16:39.800 --> 01:16:42.400
Barry is a master tracker!

01:16:42.400 --> 01:16:44.130
No doubt about it!

01:16:44.130 --> 01:16:46.410
Wanna go look a little over that way?

01:16:46.410 --> 01:16:47.580
All right.

01:16:49.130 --> 01:16:50.000
Are you all right?

01:16:58.000 --> 01:16:59.760
T-There he is.

01:17:00.050 --> 01:17:02.180
There he is! There he is! There he is! There he...

01:17:02.470 --> 01:17:07.240
We found Gabuuu!

01:17:14.850 --> 01:17:16.440
Don't let him out of your sight!

01:17:25.780 --> 01:17:27.220
Where'd they go?!

01:17:28.730 --> 01:17:30.120
That way?

01:17:30.120 --> 01:17:32.410
No, they definitely went this way!

01:17:32.410 --> 01:17:34.290
Mei, quickly!

01:17:40.800 --> 01:17:42.220
Gabu!

01:17:44.470 --> 01:17:46.860
Don't let them get away!

01:17:50.900 --> 01:17:53.900
Barry, there's no way we can get across this.

01:17:53.900 --> 01:17:56.630
Dammit, they got away?!

01:18:10.830 --> 01:18:13.320
Gabu, I'm sorry about earlier.

01:18:13.320 --> 01:18:14.290
Sorry for what?

01:18:14.290 --> 01:18:15.530
It's all right!

01:18:49.580 --> 01:18:51.670
We've really climbed a long way.

01:18:51.670 --> 01:18:52.620
Yes.

01:18:52.620 --> 01:18:54.120
And I'm tired enough to tell.

01:18:54.520 --> 01:18:57.030
Oh, you can see it over there!

01:18:57.030 --> 01:18:59.190
That's Pleasant Mountain, isn't it?

01:18:59.190 --> 01:19:00.200
It is!

01:19:00.200 --> 01:19:01.880
You can see Chomping Gorges, too.

01:19:03.680 --> 01:19:07.100
They're so small when you look at
them from up here, aren't they?

01:19:07.100 --> 01:19:10.560
We used to live in those places, didn't we?

01:19:10.560 --> 01:19:11.680
Sure did.

01:19:11.680 --> 01:19:14.850
Every day we'd chase and be chased,

01:19:14.850 --> 01:19:18.850
hide away and go searching for. It was such a pain!

01:19:20.110 --> 01:19:22.730
You really are an odd one, Gabu.

01:19:22.730 --> 01:19:24.860
You say something like that even though you're a wolf.

01:19:26.780 --> 01:19:28.490
The same goes for you, Mei.

01:19:30.860 --> 01:19:33.790
l just thought of something.

01:19:33.790 --> 01:19:34.490
What?

01:19:34.830 --> 01:19:37.660
How glad I am to have met you, Gabu.

01:19:38.040 --> 01:19:39.100
Really?

01:19:39.890 --> 01:19:42.420
I feel the same, of course...

01:19:43.830 --> 01:19:45.050
Hey, Mei.

01:19:45.050 --> 01:19:48.380
It's really there, right, the green forest?

01:19:48.380 --> 01:19:49.080
Yes.

01:19:49.710 --> 01:19:51.400
It must be.

01:19:52.180 --> 01:19:55.850
It'll be so much fun to go there.

01:19:56.350 --> 01:19:57.270
Yes.

01:19:57.270 --> 01:19:58.870
If I'm with you, Gabu...

01:20:51.150 --> 01:20:53.890
It'll clear up tomorrow, right?

01:20:55.250 --> 01:20:56.040
Yes!

01:20:56.040 --> 01:20:58.030
I'm sure the weather will be good.

01:21:33.910 --> 01:21:35.620
Mei, are you all right?

01:21:36.870 --> 01:21:38.120
Mei!

01:21:38.980 --> 01:21:40.080
It's no good.

01:21:40.790 --> 01:21:42.520
l can't walk anymore.

01:22:26.630 --> 01:22:27.880
Mei.

01:22:27.880 --> 01:22:29.650
Mei, Mei!

01:22:29.650 --> 01:22:32.510
Hang in there, please!

01:22:32.510 --> 01:22:35.880
Don't leave me alone, Mei!

01:22:47.540 --> 01:22:48.150
Mei!

01:22:49.840 --> 01:22:52.650
Thank you... Gabu.

01:22:55.360 --> 01:22:57.420
Thank goodness!

01:22:57.420 --> 01:22:59.640
Thank goodness you're alive!

01:23:00.160 --> 01:23:01.700
Mei!

01:23:27.900 --> 01:23:29.560
It's not going to let up, is it?

01:23:30.730 --> 01:23:33.460
l guess you're right.

01:23:50.220 --> 01:23:53.800
Did I just look delicious to you?

01:23:53.800 --> 01:23:54.580
Huh?

01:23:54.580 --> 01:23:55.840
N-No!

01:23:55.840 --> 01:23:57.550
Not at all!

01:23:58.480 --> 01:23:59.780
It's all right.

01:24:00.260 --> 01:24:04.230
Gabu, you haven't eaten anything for days, have you?

01:24:04.230 --> 01:24:09.560
And a goat like me can't last any
longer since it's so cold outside.

01:24:10.490 --> 01:24:11.920
So, Gabu...

01:24:12.350 --> 01:24:14.070
Live enough for the both of us.

01:24:14.070 --> 01:24:17.480
W-What are you saying?!

01:24:18.200 --> 01:24:22.700
I'm happy to have met you, Gabu.

01:24:22.700 --> 01:24:26.450
To have made a friend I would risk my life for.

01:24:26.450 --> 01:24:27.870
O-Oh...

01:24:27.870 --> 01:24:33.460
If that's how you think of me,
then I'm the one who's really happy.

01:24:33.760 --> 01:24:37.180
So Gabu, fill your belly with food,

01:24:37.180 --> 01:24:38.970
and cross this mountain in good health.

01:24:39.850 --> 01:24:41.440
What are you talking about?

01:24:41.440 --> 01:24:43.280
Where am I s'posed I find food?

01:24:44.480 --> 01:24:47.020
It's right here, isn't it?

01:24:48.800 --> 01:24:50.690
N-No!

01:24:50.690 --> 01:24:52.580
You're not food, Mei!

01:24:55.610 --> 01:24:56.270
See?

01:24:56.270 --> 01:24:57.530
No!

01:24:57.530 --> 01:24:58.850
No, no!

01:25:00.780 --> 01:25:01.870
Stop rumbling!

01:25:01.870 --> 01:25:02.860
Stop rumbling!

01:25:04.460 --> 01:25:06.540
Stop! Stop! Stop!

01:25:09.950 --> 01:25:11.380
Stop rumbling.

01:25:11.380 --> 01:25:12.960
Stop rumbling.

01:25:13.420 --> 01:25:14.890
Stop rumbling, you!

01:25:16.860 --> 01:25:19.160
Dammit!

01:25:19.160 --> 01:25:20.840
Why is it rumbling?!

01:25:23.810 --> 01:25:24.710
Gabu...

01:25:26.100 --> 01:25:32.090
Why was I born as a wolf?!

01:25:39.320 --> 01:25:40.940
Dammit...

01:25:41.910 --> 01:25:43.200
Hey, Gabu.

01:25:45.580 --> 01:25:47.150
Answer me truthfully.

01:25:48.410 --> 01:25:51.380
In that barn where you first met me...

01:25:51.380 --> 01:25:54.700
What would you have done if you knew I was a goat?

01:25:56.170 --> 01:25:57.500
l woulda eaten you.

01:25:57.500 --> 01:25:58.590
Yes.

01:25:58.590 --> 01:26:00.180
That's good.

01:26:00.180 --> 01:26:03.510
Just think of this as being like that time... okay?

01:26:08.470 --> 01:26:11.960
Really, if it was a choice between one of us surviving,

01:26:11.960 --> 01:26:16.520
or both of us starving to death, I wouldn't have a preference.

01:26:16.860 --> 01:26:23.320
Either way, we'll never be able to talk to each other again.

01:26:23.320 --> 01:26:25.530
That's what hurts me the most!

01:26:27.450 --> 01:26:28.910
l feel the same.

01:26:37.000 --> 01:26:41.560
I've been thinking of something the whole
time we've been in this blizzard.

01:26:42.300 --> 01:26:44.780
Life eventually ends.

01:26:45.510 --> 01:26:51.580
But that doesn't mean that the fact that we met,
or the time we spent together will disappear.

01:26:52.390 --> 01:26:53.120
Right?

01:26:56.440 --> 01:26:58.110
That's right.

01:26:58.110 --> 01:27:01.860
It's just a matter of how long it lasts.

01:27:06.910 --> 01:27:08.240
All right.

01:27:08.240 --> 01:27:11.370
If you put it that way, I'll do it.

01:27:11.370 --> 01:27:12.710
Oh, I know!

01:27:12.710 --> 01:27:14.880
Why don't we make it like the first time we met,

01:27:14.880 --> 01:27:18.580
where I come in from outside and just go chomp?

01:27:18.580 --> 01:27:20.480
All right, it's decided.

01:27:22.090 --> 01:27:23.680
Well, Gabu...

01:27:24.800 --> 01:27:26.000
Take care of yourself.

01:27:27.510 --> 01:27:29.090
Goodbye.

01:27:29.560 --> 01:27:30.330
Yeah.

01:27:30.330 --> 01:27:32.850
Goodbye, Mei.

01:27:39.400 --> 01:27:42.010
Goodbye, Gabu.

01:27:51.030 --> 01:27:54.660
Heh. There's no way I could eat Mei,
now that we've gone through all this.

01:28:16.340 --> 01:28:17.680
Nothing, huh?

01:28:20.860 --> 01:28:24.270
Looks like there's not a single blade of grass growing anywhere.

01:28:29.380 --> 01:28:32.140
If only we could eat snow...

01:28:35.410 --> 01:28:39.600
If he could just eat a little something,
I'm sure Mei would get his energy back!

01:28:58.730 --> 01:29:00.100
Those low-down sons of...

01:29:10.160 --> 01:29:12.110
They'd come all the way up here?

01:29:16.680 --> 01:29:21.720
<i>I'm happy to have met you, Gabu.</i>

01:29:22.880 --> 01:29:26.400
<i>To have met a friend I would risk my life for.</i>

01:29:28.370 --> 01:29:31.840
A friend you would risk your life for, huh?

01:29:43.100 --> 01:29:43.980
It's him!

01:29:43.980 --> 01:29:45.190
It's Gabu!

01:31:41.230 --> 01:31:43.310
Meiii!

01:31:44.290 --> 01:31:45.310
Gabu?

01:32:27.230 --> 01:32:28.200
Gabu?

01:32:34.270 --> 01:32:35.800
Gabu!

01:32:42.450 --> 01:32:45.140
Gabu, where did you go?

01:32:53.670 --> 01:32:55.150
T-The forest!

01:32:58.140 --> 01:32:59.090
l can see the forest!

01:32:59.770 --> 01:33:01.930
There's a green forest!

01:33:02.680 --> 01:33:03.390
Gabu!

01:33:03.390 --> 01:33:04.800
Gabu, hurry up!

01:33:05.450 --> 01:33:08.060
There really was one, Gabu!

01:33:09.230 --> 01:33:12.020
A green forest... Hurry up and come here!

01:33:12.020 --> 01:33:14.560
Gabu! Gabu!

01:33:14.560 --> 01:33:16.340
A green forest!

01:33:16.820 --> 01:33:18.040
Gabu!

01:33:18.490 --> 01:33:19.950
Gabu!

01:33:19.950 --> 01:33:21.550
Gabu!

01:33:47.910 --> 01:33:49.560
It's spring already.

01:33:50.270 --> 01:33:51.940
The flowers are blooming.

01:33:58.070 --> 01:34:00.460
l made it through the cold winter,

01:34:03.580 --> 01:34:04.710
but Gabu...

01:34:06.120 --> 01:34:07.260
What happened to you?

01:34:13.170 --> 01:34:14.610
Why won't you come here?

01:34:17.440 --> 01:34:18.360
Ah...

01:34:19.860 --> 01:34:24.080
It's all because I told him to eat me that time.

01:34:27.060 --> 01:34:29.140
If only I hadn't said such a thing...

01:34:30.160 --> 01:34:33.430
Gabu would have stayed with me.

01:34:46.530 --> 01:34:47.720
Granny.

01:34:48.910 --> 01:34:49.810
Tap.

01:34:51.060 --> 01:34:51.770
Mii.

01:34:53.420 --> 01:34:54.790
l wonder what you're all doing.

01:34:56.490 --> 01:35:00.320
l... can't go on any longer...

01:35:13.720 --> 01:35:15.860
A wolf!

01:35:15.860 --> 01:35:16.920
A wolf?

01:35:19.560 --> 01:35:21.070
A wolf!

01:35:21.860 --> 01:35:23.290
It must be Gabu!

01:35:23.290 --> 01:35:24.900
Gabu is alive.

01:35:38.780 --> 01:35:40.080
Gabu.

01:35:44.840 --> 01:35:45.840
It's Gabu!

01:36:00.530 --> 01:36:01.860
Gabu!

01:36:49.200 --> 01:36:50.120
Gabu!

01:36:50.120 --> 01:36:51.450
Thank goodness!

01:36:51.450 --> 01:36:52.680
You're alive!

01:36:59.830 --> 01:37:02.260
Hey, you're Gabu, aren't you?

01:37:02.260 --> 01:37:03.720
Where are we?

01:37:03.720 --> 01:37:05.590
What are you doing out here?

01:37:05.910 --> 01:37:07.660
Pipe down.

01:37:07.660 --> 01:37:09.640
Ain't it obvious?

01:37:09.640 --> 01:37:12.340
I'm making sure my precious food doesn't get away!

01:37:12.640 --> 01:37:13.460
Food?

01:37:14.090 --> 01:37:16.600
You're not talking about me, right?

01:37:17.920 --> 01:37:20.500
Hey, Gabu, it's me.

01:37:20.500 --> 01:37:21.640
It's Mei!

01:37:22.120 --> 01:37:25.370
Who's this "Gabu" you've been babbling about?!

01:37:25.370 --> 01:37:27.610
Do you mean me?

01:37:27.610 --> 01:37:30.850
Gabu, are you playing a joke on me?

01:37:31.460 --> 01:37:34.910
Or do you really not know who I am?

01:37:34.910 --> 01:37:36.230
Jeez.

01:37:36.230 --> 01:37:38.160
You're pretty talkative for a goat.

01:37:38.670 --> 01:37:42.560
You keep talking about "Gabu" and "Mei"
and all this stuff I don't understand,

01:37:42.560 --> 01:37:44.880
but I don't know who you are, and I don't care.

01:37:44.880 --> 01:37:48.860
'Course, I don't know who I am, either.

01:37:51.220 --> 01:37:52.380
Gabu...

01:37:53.760 --> 01:37:55.160
But you know,

01:37:56.330 --> 01:37:58.760
there's one thing I remember.

01:37:58.760 --> 01:38:00.770
W-What is it?

01:38:04.560 --> 01:38:07.310
That goat meat is my absolute favorite food!

01:38:14.540 --> 01:38:18.740
But even for a goat, you look really tasty.

01:38:19.190 --> 01:38:22.200
l could eat you whenever I please,

01:38:22.200 --> 01:38:24.250
but you're a special treat.

01:38:24.250 --> 01:38:28.130
I'm going to take my time eating you
while I watch the full moon tonight.

01:38:28.130 --> 01:38:30.200
Hey, Gabu!

01:38:30.200 --> 01:38:32.270
I'm begging you, please remember!

01:38:32.270 --> 01:38:35.090
We were friends!

01:38:35.090 --> 01:38:37.480
Cut the crap.

01:38:37.480 --> 01:38:40.880
I'm a wolf and you're a goat.

01:38:40.880 --> 01:38:42.600
Stop talking such nonsense.

01:38:43.080 --> 01:38:44.680
It's true!

01:38:45.340 --> 01:38:47.330
We went on picnics together,

01:38:48.210 --> 01:38:50.940
and we were supposed to come here together, too!

01:38:50.940 --> 01:38:54.550
Hey, Gabu, look carefully at my face!

01:38:54.550 --> 01:38:57.670
Look—we were friends, weren't we?

01:38:58.660 --> 01:39:00.420
Shut up!

01:39:00.420 --> 01:39:01.620
Give it a rest!

01:39:02.080 --> 01:39:06.810
Don't make up all these confusing stories
just 'cause you want to be spared!

01:39:09.010 --> 01:39:09.940
<i>Gabu...</i>

01:39:10.830 --> 01:39:16.120
<i>Getting caught up in that avalanche made him forget everything.</i>

01:39:48.460 --> 01:39:49.610
On the mountain,

01:39:49.970 --> 01:39:53.340
l would have been all right with being eaten by Gabu.

01:39:53.860 --> 01:39:55.010
But...

01:39:56.240 --> 01:39:58.580
you're not Gabu any longer!

01:39:58.580 --> 01:40:01.170
l don't want to be eaten by some wolf!

01:40:03.760 --> 01:40:07.140
It's been a long time since I've had a chance
to eat such a tasty-looking goat.

01:40:07.140 --> 01:40:10.190
l hope the moon comes out soon.

01:40:10.660 --> 01:40:13.140
l don't want to die like this!

01:40:14.020 --> 01:40:18.200
If this is how it was going to end, I wish
l had never met you in this forest.

01:40:18.520 --> 01:40:22.300
If this is how it was going to end, I wish
l had never crossed that mountain.

01:40:23.200 --> 01:40:26.910
If this is how it was going to end, it would have been better...

01:40:26.910 --> 01:40:31.210
It would have been better if I had never
met you on that stormy night!

01:40:32.410 --> 01:40:34.210
What... did you just say?

01:40:34.920 --> 01:40:38.220
l said, if only I had never met you on that stormy night!

01:40:39.040 --> 01:40:41.470
A stormy night?

01:40:45.900 --> 01:40:47.430
One stormy night?

01:40:48.980 --> 01:40:50.310
One stormy...

01:40:50.980 --> 01:40:52.150
night?

01:41:48.800 --> 01:41:49.490
Mei...

01:41:51.540 --> 01:41:55.170
What are you doing out here?

01:41:58.530 --> 01:41:59.500
Gabu?

01:42:06.930 --> 01:42:10.020
I've been waiting this whole time for you!

01:42:10.020 --> 01:42:11.380
Mei!

01:42:11.380 --> 01:42:12.260
Gabu!

01:42:29.660 --> 01:42:32.600
It's pretty, isn't it?

01:42:32.600 --> 01:42:35.440
Yes, it really is.

01:42:35.440 --> 01:42:41.960
I've been wanting to look at the moon
with you for a long time, Mei.

01:42:41.960 --> 01:42:43.520
Me, too.

01:42:44.050 --> 01:42:46.810
We're finally able to do it.

01:42:47.590 --> 01:42:48.760
Yeah.

01:42:49.430 --> 01:42:52.280
This is the best night ever.

01:42:53.160 --> 01:42:54.010
Gabu...

01:42:55.090 --> 01:42:59.400
We can be together forever now, can't we?

01:43:00.600 --> 01:43:05.340
We'll always... always be together!
